r through your HTTP handler. Assert a valid delivery is committed, an invalid signature writes nothing, and redelivery does not fulfill twice. Force a repository error after the audit write and prove the whole transaction rolls back. Test two concurrent deliveries against your real database, not just an in-memory repository.",[484,1349,1350,1351,1354],{},"For subscription access, cover a future grace end, a past end, resume clearing the date, and nonpayment cancellation. For orders, cover initial payment, renewal, duplicate delivery, and a reversal without changing ",[488,1352,1353],{},"paid"," to a made-up status.",[892,1356,1358],{"id":1357},"exercise-the-vatly-sandbox","Exercise the Vatly sandbox",[484,1360,1361,1362,1365,1366,1369,1370,1373],{},"With a test key, ",[488,1363,1364],{},"testHelpers()->advanceRenewal($id)",", ",[488,1367,1368],{},"forceRenewalPaid($id)",", and ",[488,1371,1372],{},"forceRenewalFailed($id, 'card_expired')"," advance real test-mode state and provoke webhooks. Unlike the fakes above, these make remote writes. Use them only in a dedicated sandbox integration test, never with live records.",[484,1375,1376,1377,1383,1384,1151],{},"For sandbox fields, see the ",[1378,1379,293],"a",{"href":1380,"rel":1381},"https:\u002F\u002Fdocs.vatly.com\u002Fapi-reference",[1382],"nofollow",". For receiver design, see ",[1378,1385,50],{"href":210},[1387,1388,1389],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sbssI, html code.shiki .sbssI{--shiki-light:#F76D47;--shiki-default:#F78C6C;--shiki-dark:#F78C6C}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF